WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.126 --> 00:00:03.029
- My next guest is crazy talented.

00:00:03.029 --> 00:00:04.198
I mean, he's written so many songs

00:00:04.198 --> 00:00:06.040
you don't even know he's written them.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.487
He sold more than 20
million albums worldwide

00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:10.593
and won three Grammys not too shabby.

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:13.136
Now he's back as a judge
every Tuesday evening

00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:16.261
on the hit NBC show, my
sister's favorite show,

00:00:16.261 --> 00:00:18.136
World Of Dance, check it out.

00:00:18.136 --> 00:00:21.553
(dramatic electronic music)

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:26.202
- Yeah.

00:00:27.085 --> 00:00:28.252
Hey, hey, hey.

00:00:41.642 --> 00:00:43.193
- All right y'all, give it up for Ne-Yo!

00:00:43.193 --> 00:00:44.905
Hey, what's up Ne-Yo, how you doing?

00:00:44.905 --> 00:00:45.738
- How are you, love?

00:00:45.738 --> 00:00:46.696
Good to see you.

00:00:46.696 --> 00:00:48.274
- I am hanging in there.

00:00:48.274 --> 00:00:49.174
I think we're all just,

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.669
it's a crazy year this year.

00:00:51.669 --> 00:00:53.596
- To say the least, yeah, yeah.

00:00:53.596 --> 00:00:56.362
- Yeah, it's a lot, but
it's nice to see you again.

00:00:56.362 --> 00:00:58.032
And how have you actually been handling

00:00:58.032 --> 00:00:59.758
the craziness, all the lockdown?

00:00:59.758 --> 00:01:01.254
'Cause you've kids with you.

00:01:01.254 --> 00:01:04.300
- Yeah, yeah I have
four beautiful children,

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.700
four very loud, very energetic children.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:07.533
- [Kelly] Yeah. (chuckles)

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.516
- And they are thoroughly enjoying

00:01:09.516 --> 00:01:11.307
all the downtime with dad,

00:01:11.307 --> 00:01:12.925
they really truly are.

00:01:12.925 --> 00:01:14.921
And to be honest, I am too, I am too.

00:01:14.921 --> 00:01:17.336
I mean, my condolences and my heart

00:01:17.336 --> 00:01:19.543
goes out to anybody that lost anybody

00:01:19.543 --> 00:01:21.713
to COVID, and the whole situation.

00:01:21.713 --> 00:01:24.944
But as far as the quarantine,

00:01:24.944 --> 00:01:27.789
I'm rarely at home anyway,
I travel a whole lot,

00:01:27.789 --> 00:01:29.463
and this was kind of an opportunity

00:01:29.463 --> 00:01:33.637
for me to kinda, like
reconnect with my kids.

00:01:33.637 --> 00:01:36.482
You know, I don't know
if you knew personally,

00:01:36.482 --> 00:01:38.279
but you know, before quarantine,

00:01:38.279 --> 00:01:40.748
you know me and my wife
were talking divorce,

00:01:40.748 --> 00:01:43.062
but the quarantine kind
of allowed us the time

00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:46.510
to sit down and really kind
of lock back into each other.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.343
So like.
- Wow!

00:01:47.343 --> 00:01:48.847
- We're good now, there's
no divorce happening,

00:01:48.847 --> 00:01:49.680
everything's good.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.346
- Oh, wow!
- But yeah man!

00:01:51.346 --> 00:01:55.265
Again it almost feels wrong to say that

00:01:55.265 --> 00:01:58.697
this whole COVID-19 quarantine thing

00:01:58.697 --> 00:02:00.119
was kind of a blessing to me.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.244
- Wow, what a beautiful thing

00:02:01.244 --> 00:02:03.125
that it ended up working out.

00:02:03.125 --> 00:02:04.998
And you took such a negative situation,

00:02:04.998 --> 00:02:07.199
it could have been a really negative thing

00:02:07.199 --> 00:02:09.113
and made it a positive with this pandemic

00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:10.375
and everything going on.

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:11.208
- Absolutely.

00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:13.008
- But on another positive
that you've just released

00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:15.057
a song called "U 2 Luv."

00:02:15.057 --> 00:02:16.805
- U 2 Luv!
- What is it about?

00:02:16.805 --> 00:02:18.073
And what is the inspiration?

00:02:18.073 --> 00:02:19.862
Is it your life?

00:02:19.862 --> 00:02:21.957
- So "U 2 Luv," featuring Jeremih,

00:02:21.957 --> 00:02:23.777
by the way, shout out to Jeremih.

00:02:23.777 --> 00:02:26.110
The song basically is about,

00:02:27.791 --> 00:02:30.397
the tagline is I only want you to love,

00:02:30.397 --> 00:02:31.713
I don't want nobody else.

00:02:31.713 --> 00:02:33.027
So it's basically just talking about

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:35.221
you and that one person and mind you,

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.547
we recorded the song before
the quarantine happened.

00:02:38.547 --> 00:02:40.366
But considering the quarantine,

00:02:40.366 --> 00:02:43.111
it's kinda like the perfect quarantine bay

00:02:43.111 --> 00:02:44.436
to playing the song you know what I mean.

00:02:44.436 --> 00:02:45.269
(laughs)

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:46.978
You and the quarantine bae.

00:02:46.978 --> 00:02:47.811
- Yeah!
- Sitting in front

00:02:47.811 --> 00:02:49.703
of the couch with this
plan in the background,

00:02:49.703 --> 00:02:51.951
it's just a perfect scene,
it makes perfect sense.

00:02:51.951 --> 00:02:53.292
- Yeah, all right!

00:02:53.292 --> 00:02:54.936
Okay, so you did something

00:02:54.936 --> 00:02:57.022
that I like vowed to never do again,

00:02:57.022 --> 00:02:59.701
because this is a very hard thing to do.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.324
I've sang at a few funerals in my life.

00:03:02.324 --> 00:03:03.157
- Whoa!

00:03:03.157 --> 00:03:06.265
- And it's just the hardest scenario ever

00:03:06.265 --> 00:03:08.580
if you know them or if you
don't, it doesn't matter.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.725
Because you're seeing other
people's pain regardless,

00:03:10.725 --> 00:03:11.903
and it's just painful.

00:03:11.903 --> 00:03:12.736
- Yeah!

00:03:12.736 --> 00:03:14.837
- But you actually performed
at George Floyd's funeral.

00:03:14.837 --> 00:03:15.670
- [Ne-Yo] Yeah.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.740
- [Kelly] So how did you get involved?

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.362
- [Ne-Yo] I believe that
the family reached out.

00:03:19.362 --> 00:03:21.306
I got the information from my manager,

00:03:21.306 --> 00:03:23.081
so I didn't speak directly to the family,

00:03:23.081 --> 00:03:24.410
but I believe they reached out

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.513
and asked if I would sing.

00:03:26.513 --> 00:03:29.273
And, I mean of course I said, "Yeah."

00:03:29.273 --> 00:03:31.213
So we got down there,

00:03:31.213 --> 00:03:34.654
I tried to sit a little
further back, you know,

00:03:34.654 --> 00:03:38.379
'cause I didn't want the
moment to be about me at all.

00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:39.212
You know what I mean?

00:03:39.212 --> 00:03:40.534
Like I didn't wanna do
the celebrity thing,

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:41.570
I didn't want that.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.453
But when they saw me,

00:03:42.453 --> 00:03:43.593
they pulled me off to a closer pew

00:03:43.593 --> 00:03:45.374
and I'm like, "All
right, all right, cool."

00:03:45.374 --> 00:03:48.991
So I'm sitting there
and I get up on stage,

00:03:48.991 --> 00:03:50.643
and the second I got up
there I look in the audience,

00:03:50.643 --> 00:03:52.888
and his daughter sitting
right in front of me.

00:03:52.888 --> 00:03:56.524
And then all I could see in
that moment was my daughter.

00:03:56.524 --> 00:03:59.894
And it broke, I broke, I couldn't.

00:03:59.894 --> 00:04:02.374
- It's the hardest thing to do.

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:03.207
- Yeah.
- This thing...

00:04:03.207 --> 00:04:04.565
- I couldn't get my words together

00:04:04.565 --> 00:04:07.169
with what I wanted to
say, that came out wrong.

00:04:07.169 --> 00:04:08.002
Some people misunderstood,

00:04:08.002 --> 00:04:09.668
what I meant by that whatever.

00:04:09.668 --> 00:04:12.103
- I know that's kind of the bad thing too.

00:04:12.103 --> 00:04:13.336
'Cause I feel like,

00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:15.939
I heard there was a bit of
blow back from the funeral.

00:04:15.939 --> 00:04:17.493
Did that hit you hard

00:04:17.493 --> 00:04:20.024
to where you were like, "Wait,
that was totally missed.

00:04:20.024 --> 00:04:22.010
I got, that was twisted."?

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.521
- You know what, initially, I won't lie.

00:04:24.521 --> 00:04:26.265
Initially it did 'cause I'll be honest.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:29.848
When my manager called
me and told me about,

00:04:29.848 --> 00:04:31.441
what was being said or whatever,

00:04:31.441 --> 00:04:33.954
and I instantly got upset like, What?

00:04:33.954 --> 00:04:36.185
Like how could anybody really think

00:04:36.185 --> 00:04:38.507
that I would stand up
at this man's funeral

00:04:38.507 --> 00:04:40.193
in front of this man's family,

00:04:40.193 --> 00:04:43.710
and mean anything negative or wrong about,

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.339
like how could anybody make that mistake?

00:04:46.339 --> 00:04:47.185
Right, so.
- Yeah.

00:04:47.185 --> 00:04:49.230
- So, I got upset and my response was,

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.837
you know what, intelligent
people know what I meant.

00:04:51.837 --> 00:04:52.670
- Yeah.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.285
- And anybody ignorant,
I ain't worried about it.

00:04:54.285 --> 00:04:56.013
But then my manager had to catch me.

00:04:56.013 --> 00:04:56.904
He was like,

00:04:56.904 --> 00:04:59.053
no, that's not what this is.

00:04:59.053 --> 00:05:02.277
This moment is really,
really important, okay?

00:05:02.277 --> 00:05:05.015
The least you could do
is take a few minutes

00:05:05.015 --> 00:05:06.638
to make sure that people understand

00:05:06.638 --> 00:05:08.506
what it is you're saying, okay?

00:05:08.506 --> 00:05:10.169
Because ignorance is division.

00:05:10.169 --> 00:05:11.535
And we don't need division
right now, all right?

00:05:11.535 --> 00:05:12.933
We need to do this right now.

00:05:12.933 --> 00:05:13.766
- Wow!

00:05:13.766 --> 00:05:14.895
- So take a second.

00:05:14.895 --> 00:05:16.414
Explain what it is you meant,

00:05:16.414 --> 00:05:19.342
not because anyone is owed an explanation,

00:05:19.342 --> 00:05:20.885
but because it's the right thing to do

00:05:20.885 --> 00:05:24.750
in order for unity to be
part of the narrative,

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.870
not division, you know?

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.041
So I took it upon myself,
I went into the comments

00:05:29.041 --> 00:05:30.270
and I answered some people.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.810
Somebody said, "He wasn't
sacrificed, he was murdered."

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.698
And I'm like, okay well,

00:05:36.698 --> 00:05:38.387
in the realm of a lot of sacrifices,

00:05:38.387 --> 00:05:40.641
they kind of involve death, I mean,

00:05:40.641 --> 00:05:44.198
it's unfortunate that his death was

00:05:44.198 --> 00:05:45.889
the spark that caused this energy

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:48.663
that is slowly but surely
creating change for us.

00:05:48.663 --> 00:05:51.308
But the truth of the
matter is this man's life

00:05:51.308 --> 00:05:53.449
was sacrificed in order
for this to happen.

00:05:53.449 --> 00:05:54.907
Now I don't think that was

00:05:54.907 --> 00:05:57.003
the reasoning behind it initially,

00:05:57.003 --> 00:05:58.886
of course, the cops killed him

00:05:58.886 --> 00:06:01.922
and it was meant for wicked.

00:06:01.922 --> 00:06:04.479
But we then took something
that was meant for wicked

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:06.075
and turned it into a positive.

00:06:06.075 --> 00:06:07.742
- Yeah, no, I agree.

00:06:08.752 --> 00:06:10.721
You're such a great man,

00:06:10.721 --> 00:06:12.730
you're such a good dude, it's so cool.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.448
I am back with Ne-Yo, and you can see him

00:06:14.448 --> 00:06:15.281
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:15.281 --> 00:06:18.328
- On World Of Dance Tuesdays on NBC,

00:06:18.328 --> 00:06:20.497
seriously, my sister is
obsessed with your show.

00:06:20.497 --> 00:06:21.950
(chuckles)

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.824
So have you been missing your
friends at World Of Dance?

00:06:23.824 --> 00:06:25.528
Have you been missing Derek and J-Lo?

00:06:25.528 --> 00:06:27.364
- Yeah, man, I really truly have,

00:06:27.364 --> 00:06:28.197
- Yeah!

00:06:28.197 --> 00:06:29.072
- So here's the thing.

00:06:29.072 --> 00:06:30.372
So the show is not live.

00:06:30.372 --> 00:06:33.236
Okay, that's no secret to
anyone, the show is not live.

00:06:33.236 --> 00:06:36.500
We shot the last show, the
season finale, pretty much

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.180
the day that this whole
COVID-19 madness began,

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.013
- Lucky!

00:06:41.013 --> 00:06:43.050
- The day that they started
sending people home,

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.485
was the day that we shot the final show.

00:06:45.485 --> 00:06:48.900
So we decided that for the
first half of the show,

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.352
we wanted to break it down,

00:06:50.352 --> 00:06:53.195
like we wanted to make
the contestants earned

00:06:53.195 --> 00:06:56.486
that big beautiful stage with
the LED screen and all that,

00:06:56.486 --> 00:06:57.518
we wanted to make them earn that.

00:06:57.518 --> 00:07:00.944
So the qualifier rounds
and the dual rounds

00:07:00.944 --> 00:07:03.004
are all done in a warehouse.

00:07:03.004 --> 00:07:05.920
Now, I think we're a little
bit ahead of our time,

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.723
(child wailing)
Hey, hold on buddy, hold on.

00:07:07.723 --> 00:07:08.814
(chuckles)

00:07:08.814 --> 00:07:09.772
I think we were,

00:07:09.772 --> 00:07:10.605
a little bit ahead of time because,

00:07:10.605 --> 00:07:11.438
sort of qualifying rounds.

00:07:12.382 --> 00:07:13.571
- [Child] Oh, hi!

00:07:13.571 --> 00:07:15.486
